# Repo-root line-ending policy (cross-platform, kit 1.50.2).
# Rationale: a CRLF that sneaks into a `.sh`/`.py` breaks its shebang on Linux
# (`bad interpreter: ...^M`), and a BOM before a shebang makes the kernel hand the file
# to /bin/sh -> exit 2 -> a PreToolUse guard silently blocks every tool call. Both were
# field-measured; this file makes them structurally impossible. Last matching rule wins.

# Everything is text, normalized to LF in the repo.
* text=auto eol=lf

# PowerShell stays CRLF: Windows PowerShell 5.1 (shipped with Windows) mishandles a
# .ps1 that is not CRLF. These are the only files that must NOT be LF.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Golden fixtures are binary field-truth: an approval suite is bytes a human signed off,
# never re-encoded. The repo has none today; this is a guard for when tests add them
# (the shipped template `uscha-kit/templates/.gitattributes` carries the same for user repos).
*.approved   binary
*.received   binary
*.approved.* binary
*.received.* binary

# Binary assets never get EOL/whitespace touched.
*.png  binary
*.pdf  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.webp binary
# site pages: LF only (D-6, judges panel 2026-08-19)
site/**/*.html text eol=lf
site/*.txt text eol=lf
site/*.sh text eol=lf
